    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the interface counters on the hop 2 link and the error counts aren't really spiking, but the jitter is still all over the place during peak hours. it's almost like something is randomly interfering with the signal. could it be more of a hardware-level issue, like a failing transceiver or something weirdly intermittent like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the interface counters are clean, but the jitter is still erratic during peak times, a failing transceiver is certainly a possibility, though it often presents with more consistent CRC errors. It could also be related to buffer exhaustion or micro-bursts on the upstream device, which are hard to catch with standard counter checks. I'd suggest looking at the queue depth statistics on hop 2's device during those peak periods. If those queues are constantly overflowing or spiking, it points to congestion, even if the interface errors aren't visible yet.",
